# XCUITest destination

When running, debugging, or suggesting XCUITests for this repo:

- **Always** target the real plugged-in device named **iPhone** (iPhone 12) on this machine.
- **Never** use `platform=iOS Simulator` for UI tests (`ios-xq-finance-app-ui-tests` / `AppUITests`).
- Unit tests (`ios-xq-finance-app` / `AppTests`) may still use the Simulator.
- IPA archive and device reinstall checks use **David 🥷** (iPhone Air) — see `scripts/archive-ipa.sh`.

## How to run

Prefer the device script:

```bash
./scripts/run-device-ui-tests.sh
```

Or resolve UDID then pass it to `xcodebuild`:

```bash
DEVICE_ID="$(IOS_DEVICE_NAME=iPhone ./scripts/plugged-iphone-udid.sh)"
xcodebuild \
  -project ios-xq-finance-app.xcodeproj \
  -scheme ios-xq-finance-app-ui-tests \
  -destination "platform=iOS,id=${DEVICE_ID}" \
  DEVELOPMENT_TEAM="${DEVELOPMENT_TEAM:-T99X93V7Y2}" \
  -allowProvisioningUpdates \
  test
```

Optional overrides: `IOS_DEVICE_NAME="iPhone"` or `IOS_DEVICE_ID=<udid>`.

## Preconditions

- Cable connected, phone unlocked and trusted
- Only one physical iPhone connected, or set `IOS_DEVICE_NAME` / `IOS_DEVICE_ID`
- If the runner hangs after “Initiating session”, unlock the phone and dismiss any Automation / Developer Mode prompts

## In Xcode

Scheme: `ios-xq-finance-app-ui-tests` → destination **iPhone** (physical iPhone 12), not a Simulator.
